Draw emoji-presentation text in HarmonyOS's colour emoji font.

Skia's custom font managers understand CJK language tags and nothing else:
asked for a character with "und-Zsye", the tag Blink adds for emoji
presentation, they return the first font that has it. A keycap emoji
("0", U+FE0F, U+20E3) is asked for with its digit, which HarmonyOS Sans --
or the user's theme font -- has, so the sequence was shaped in a text font
and U+20E3 drew as a box (ArkWeb draws the keycap).

OhosFontManager now sends emoji-presentation requests to the system's colour
emoji fonts first, as Android's font manager does, and wraps the system
manager even when no theme font is set (the theme side is then empty) --
it used to exist only with a theme font, so most phones never reached it.
When the directory scan leaves the emoji fonts out of the family list, the
"*Emoji*" files in the font directories are loaded directly. What was found
is logged once per process.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-emoji-font-fallback.patch

